  "gatingReading": "losslessLocator.maxEdgeDeltaPx == 0 AND |alignment.subPixelOffset| < 1px on both axes AND the 2px probe still reads >=2px",
  "gatingReadingChangedByNode4": {
    "was": "alignment.bestOffset == [0,0] AND losslessLocator.maxEdgeDeltaPx <= 1",
    "why": "Two changes, one stricter and one honest. STRICTER: the locator must now read exactly 0 on every edge, not <=1, which is tighter than the plan's own threshold. HONEST: the displacement search steps in whole pixels, so its argmin cannot distinguish 'moved 1px' from 'same pixel, resampled with a 0.55px phase difference'. neg-top is the second kind — its locator reads 0 on all four edges while the argmin flips to 1 because the parabola's vertex sits at +0.55. Holding a whole-pixel instrument to a sub-pixel claim is what the old wording did; the refined offset is the same measurement read at its real resolution.",
    "disclosure": "This is a criterion change that turns a FAIL into a PASS and is called out as such in results/report.md. The plan's threshold (per-edge <=1px on the magenta locator) is met at 0px on all six cases either way; what changed is an extra gate node #3 invented that was stricter than any instrument here can support."
  },
  "instrumentNote": "The production encoder writes 4:2:0. Every box here lands on an odd coordinate or has an odd contained height, so the magenta locator's outer column shares a chroma sample with the background and a threshold-located edge reads up to 1px early. That is the instrument, not the geometry: the same commands rendered losslessly at 4:4:4 read exactly. Both numbers are reported.",
  "displayCanvasProbe": {
    "canvas": {
      "width": 853,
      "height": 480
    },
    "meaning": "DD-2's irreducible residual, measured PNG-vs-PNG so no codec is involved: the preview draws on a display-sized canvas, so the box lands on the export grid in NORMALISED space and what is left is the display scale itself. Evidence only — not gating."
  },
